B.bdq=new A.F(B.eb,B.eb)
B.bdr=new A.F("Choose who marches off.",B.x)
B.bds=new A.F("Players."," Up to four can share a campaign on one device: at the realm choice, set Players (top right) and tap a realm for each, in the order you play. The other realms are the AI. Scenarios are for one player.")
B.bdt=new A.F("","The Danes and the Norwegians start at war with every other realm, with war-fleets already on the coast.")
B.bdv=new A.F("Medals."," Your wins are kept on this device. On the realm choice each realm shows a gold mark for each difficulty you have won with it (Easy, Normal, Hard), a crown for a High King win, and its fastest win in turns. Each scenario shows its own.")
B.bdw=new A.F("","Attacking or pillaging a realm you are not at war with declares war \u2014 but not while a peace still holds.")
B.bdy=new A.F(0.7,B.oo)
B.bdA=new A.F("","Your armies join only when one marches onto another, or when you press Combine. A longer march passes your armies by, and joins one only where it ends (not one fortifying or ordered to attack). Armies standing in the same province defend it together.")
B.bdB=new A.F("","Then they pay 50% more tax and give more men, and your armies fight 10% harder among them.")
B.bdD=new A.F("Play on."," When a realm wins the crown and yours still stands, you may play on in the same campaign, for High King.")
B.bdE=new A.F("A last stand:"," once a game, if your realm is down to 2 provinces or fewer after holding 4 or more, 60 men gather in your strongest province to fight on, free.")
B.aI9=new A.F(B.K,B.bg)
B.aIa=new A.F(B.aC,B.aX)
B.bdH=new A.F("Danegeld:"," when the Danes are much stronger than you and their hosts stand at your border, they demand half your treasury (at least 100 gold) for 8 turns of peace. It only buys time: when the peace runs out, they come back. East Anglia, the land they came for, is never offered terms. Playing the Danes, you can demand Danegeld yourself.")
B.bdL=new A.F("Attacks are orders"," fought when you end the turn. Each army fights one battle a turn, and armies sent against the same province fight as one host. A realm's province with no army in it is still defended by the levies it musters.")
B.bdN=new A.F("","Playing Scotland, you start with a 6-turn truce with the Norwegians.")
B.aRd=new A.q(1,0.1843137254901961,0.37254901960784315,0.6588235294117647,B.f)
B.bdR=new A.F(0.5,B.aRd)
B.bdS=new A.F("High King:"," you win when every rival realm has fallen or submitted to you. Nobody wins by size, the Danelaw or a homeland.")
B.bdT=new A.F("Recruit more troops",!1)
B.bdU=new A.F("YOUR TRIBUTARY",B.j)
B.bdV=new A.F("When turn 8 ends,"," the Danes' Great Heathen Army lands on East Anglia's coast \u2014 the kingdom they come to take (anywhere on England's east coast when you play East Anglia).")
B.bdW=new A.F("Longer marches:"," tap a province farther away to see the road there, then tap it again (or March here) to send the army. It sets out at once and goes on at the start of each of your turns, by the fastest road through your own or an ally's land (by sea too, if it has ships). A dotted line shows the selected army's road, and a flag marks where each march ends. It stops beside land it may not enter, or when its road is blocked or an enemy host stands in the way: attacking is up to you. Stop march, Fortify or a new order ends a march.")
B.bdX=new A.F("Tap an army"," to select it. Green provinces are ones it can march into \u2014 your own or an ally's. Red ones marked with crossed swords can be attacked.")
B.bdY=new A.F("The end."," Victory is checked when every player has played; a tie goes to the larger realm, then the earlier seat. After a crown, every player still standing may play on. A player whose realm falls is told so once and then passed over. The end screen shows each player's saga. Wins in a game of several players earn no medals.")
B.bdZ=new A.F(null,"They refuse.")
B.be0=new A.F("Gold"," comes from taxes \u2014 the more people, the more gold \u2014 and from markets, ports and mines. Manpower comes from your people, and more from barracks.")
B.be1=new A.F(B.ae,B.b1)
B.be2=new A.F(0.3,B.oo)
B.be5=new A.F("Pillage"," a province your army stands in or borders: not your own or an ally's, not one guarded by another realm's army, and only if your men outnumber its levies, who fight back.")
B.be6=new A.F("No goal:"," nobody wins. Rule as long as you like. Playing for High King or no goal, you may end the campaign from the game menu.")
B.be8=new A.F("Turns."," Each plays a whole turn in seat order, then the AI realms move. Between turns the screen covers the map: pass the device, and the next player taps to begin. Each sees only their own realm through the fog, and is told what happened since their last turn.")
B.be9=new A.F(B.a8,B.b1)
B.bea=new A.F("The coalition:"," from turn 6, if you come close to the crown (whatever the goal), the other realms make peace among themselves and all go to war with you until you fall back. The panel at the top left says when; on Hard it comes sooner. It can turn on a runaway rival too.")
B.beb=new A.F("A scattered start"," (chosen when you pick your realm) gives every realm one random province with a Barracks and a small host; the rest is independent. No great Viking host lands; for the Crown, only the conquest goal counts.")
B.bec=new A.F("Between players."," Players keep a truce for their first 4 turns; then realms that were at war in 793 are at war again. Peace and alliances are proposed from the Realms screen and answered on the other's turn; no Danegeld, submission or ransom passes between players, and a king is never another player's captive. A battle between players is decided at once, with no charge or retreat.")
B.bed=new A.F("2 moves a turn:"," march twice, or march and then attack. Marching into highland takes both moves.")
B.bef=new A.F(null,"No active game")
B.bei=new A.F("","Now and then an event card asks you to choose.")
B.bek=new A.F("","The handshake button at the top right opens the realms of Britain.")
B.bel=new A.F("Scenarios"," are short set pieces from history: choose Scenarios at the top of the realm choice. Each gives you a realm, its year, its own goal and a turn limit. The goal and the turns left show at the top left.")
B.bem=new A.F("Both keep the morale, veterancy and moves left.",B.x)
B.n0=new A.Kz(0,"left")
B.n1=new A.Kz(1,"right")
B.ben=new A.F(B.n0,B.n1)
B.beo=new A.F("The Crown: rule 45 provinces."," Every realm wins this way.")
B.aIb=new A.tx(null,null)
B.mI=new A.dJ(4,"scrollLeft")
B.mJ=new A.dJ(8,"scrollRight")
B.ber=new A.F(B.mI,B.mJ)
B.bet=new A.F(B.mJ,B.mI)
B.beu=new A.F("Build:"," a Farm makes the population grow faster, a Market or Port brings gold, and so does a Mine where there is ore (the highlands, Cornwall, parts of Wales, the Pennines and the Mendips: +10 gold a turn); a Barracks lets you recruit there, and a Fortification makes the province hard to take.")
B.bev=new A.F(!1,!1)
B.bew=new A.F(!1,null)
B.bex=new A.F(!1,!0)
B.bey=new A.F("Wales and Scotland"," can instead hold every province they started with and win 27 more.")
B.mE=new A.dJ(16,"scrollUp")
B.mG=new A.dJ(32,"scrollDown")
B.bez=new A.F(B.mE,B.mG)
B.beA=new A.F("Walls:"," assault a fortified province (its defenders fight 30% harder per wall level), or besiege it \u2014 it falls in a few turns if your army stays beside it. Besieging a realm you are at peace with is war.")
B.beB=new A.F("The loot"," comes from its markets and farms, which burn (a Market is worth 60 gold a level, a Farm 30), and a little from its people. Walls, barracks, ports and mines are left standing. Some of its people die, and the land lies charred for a few turns. It takes the army's whole turn, and starts a war if you were not at war (you are asked first).")
B.beC=new A.F("When you are attacked,"," SALLY OUT is your charge, and ABANDON gives up the province to save your men: its levies fall back to a neighbouring province you hold.")
B.beE=new A.F("","You lose if another realm wins first, or if you lose all your land and armies. The panel at the top left shows how far you have come and the rival closest to winning.")
B.beF=new A.F(B.K,B.aC)
B.beH=new A.F("","Each turn is one season, four to a year, starting in spring 793.")
B.beI=new A.F("AT PEACE",B.x)
B.beK=new A.F("","Your starting provinces also build on their own, with part of your spare gold.")
B.aIc=new A.F(null,B.i)
B.beL=new A.F(B.mG,B.mE)
B.beM=new A.F("Every realm can sail."," A host with ships, on the coast and not yet moved this turn, can sail to a coast within reach and march, attack or pillage there. The voyage takes its whole turn. One ship is enough, and a beaten host with ships that has nowhere to fall back to on land escapes by sea.")
B.beP=new A.F("Only the army with ships can sail.",B.dv)
B.beR=new A.F("","When you choose your realm, you choose the goal too: the Crown, High King, or no goal.")
B.beT=new A.F("Leave at least one man behind.",B.N)
B.beU=new A.F("Battles are live."," Troops and morale fall round by round. CHARGE! is a gamble: it can break a wavering enemy, but against a strong, steady line many of your men fall. Pulling back is free before the lines meet (CALL OFF) and costly after (RETREAT). A side whose morale reaches zero breaks and is cut down.")
B.beV=new A.F("ALLIED",B.bS)
B.beW=new A.F(B.a8,B.ae)
B.beX=new A.F(!0,!1)
B.beY=new A.F(!0,!0)
B.beZ=new A.F(B.n1,B.n0)
B.bf0=new A.F("End Turn"," when your orders are given. Your attacks are fought first; then the other realms move (the map replays their moves), and you defend against their attacks.")
B.bf2=new A.F("Colonize"," a province whose people are of another culture or religion: your settlers make them your own in 5 turns, for gold (more for a crowded province).")
B.aId=new A.F(B.K,B.a8)
B.bf3=new A.F("Recruit"," in a province of yours with a Barracks. Soldiers cost gold and manpower, and each people fields its own kinds of troops.")
B.bf4=new A.F(u.X,!1)
